n see tom holland  spider-man not touch him at all so it  wasn't him and he's not just turning his  head you can very clearly see that he is  getting hit here now some people are  claiming that it's one of the poles that  hit him but if you look really closely  and slow it down you can see that no  pole actually hits him there is a pole  behind him that looks like it's actually  going to hit him but then his face moves  way before the pole actually does plus  if you take a look at how his head goes  back you can clearly tell that he is  getting punched it looks like it's a  left hook or possibly a kick from the  left side it's a really high impact hit  so it's not him turning his head for  whatever reason that's off the table  that's not what's happening and a pole i  don't think would do that damage plus  again if you look closely no poles  actually hit him or at least cause this  initial jerk to the left what's actually  happening here is another spider-man  actually hit him he's just been edited  out of this frame we know that toby and  andrew are going to show up probably  within the last 30 minutes of the movie  and this scene is definitely towards the  end so this is probably a 3v3 fight the  three spider-man vs electro sandman and  the lizard and more evidence for this is  if you take a look at the direction that  the lizard and electro are going they're  not actually going towards tom hall and  spider-man but the other two aren't  electro is too high and he looks to be a  little bit to the right and then the  lizard is a little bit to the bottom and  to the left it's pretty clear that  they're not leaping to attack tom  holland's spider-man but they're  actually leaping to attack another  spider-man now more evidence for this  which i didn't talk about yesterday is  the fact that they're on the statue of  liberty and we can see the scaffolding  from the leaked pictures of andrew  garfield now i'm only showing these  pictures because they've just been out  there forever now but if we take a look  at the statue of liberty we see a bunch  of scaffolding on it and in this  particular scene where we see tom  holland i actually believe he is talking  to andrew garfield and toby maguire why  because the background is exactly the  same from the leaked photos we have a  couple of bars behind him and the ocean  in the background because we know this  takes place on the bay we now know it  takes place on top of the statue of  liberty which we didn't know before by  the scaffolding photos but this scene  right here with tom holland the  background is exactly the same as the  background for the leaked andrew  garfield and tobin maguire photos this  is a scene where they're all talking to  each other most likely before that fight  with the lizard electro and sandman or  after this is possibly the biggest  confirmation  right here a scene of tom in the exact  same place that the leaked photos of  andrew and toby are at that point it's  pretty hard to deny the evidence but  wait there's more we have more evidence  many eagle-eyed fans have spotted what  we believe to be andrew garfield's arm  in one of the scenes now it looks like  he's kind of been edited out but not  completely it looks pretty clear in the  scene where ned is trying to catch mj as  she's following that there is a  spider-man in the background it looks  like we can see one of their arms and it  literally looks like it's halfway edited  out like they edited most of it but got  lazy or got tired they're probably  working very very hard and working a lot  of hours and just didn't finish it and  somehow that slid under the bus but i am  actually hoping that it is andrew  garfield's arm because it looks like he  might have a chance to kind of get  redemption from that gwen stacy fall  perhaps he actually goes on to save mj  now the hand that we see going to catch  her does indeed look like tom holland's  hand and i have two theories about this  well three because the first one is just  a normal fact that tom holland is  actually going to save her the other  theory is it's actually andrew's hand  the entire time and he's the one that  saves her or it could be tom holland's  hand but he misses her but andrew sweeps  in and ends up saving her in the end now  i know some people might not like this  my buddy greg if the real rejects  pointed out that he would actually like  to see tom hall and spider-man save her  he'd like to see him do something and i  totally understand that but i personally  would really love to see andrew garfield  get a sort of redemption here by saving  mj now there's more evidence and it's  another scene that takes place once  again on the statue of liberty and i  stress this because i do believe that  this scene with the statue of liberty is  where all three spider-man do come  together i believe it's a big fight with  all of them many of you may have seen  this by now but it's a picture of  spider-man swinging through the  scaffolding of the statue of liberty  made to look like tom holland spider-man  but is it we could actually be looking  at toby mcguire spider-man or andrew  garfield spider-man in this picture  because it looks like somebody tried to  cover up the suit making it look like  tom holland's suit but forgot to edit  the eyes because the eyes do not look  like tom holland's spider-man eyes these  eyes are too big to be tom holland's  spider-man's eyes his eyes are smaller  than this but andrew garfield's and toby  maguire's eyes are much bigger these  actually look like they could be toby's  they replaced the entire suit but the  eyes perhaps maybe they thought people  wouldn't notice or perhaps maybe they  knew that we would but didn't care  anyways and wanted us to find out now  it's important to note that us marvel  fans aren't strangers to trailers being  edited to keep us surprised they did it  for infinity war they did it for end  game they've done it for other trailers  as well and it's actually kind of nice  in most cases unfortunately for sony and  spiderman no way home a lot of things  have leaked out otherwise normally most  things are kept pretty secretive at  marvel studios but remember the hulk and  wakanda that's the most infamous trailer  editing scene that we've had so far we  never got the hulk and infinity war we  got the hulkbuster but never the hulk  and we especially did not see the hulk  running with the rest of the avengers in  wakanda the trailer was edited and it  definitely looks like this trailer is  edited as well specifically because some  of the scenes involving the statue of  liberty and that scaffolding have toby  maguire and andrew garfield in it and  the studios made a decision to not show  them in the trailer and not even tease  them although they were kind of teased  doc ock said you're not peter but he did  say hello peter at first this of course  is because his peter parker is tobey  maguire's peter parker so therefore he  acknowledged tobey maguire's peter  parker in this scene there's literally  zero reasons for them to bring in the  villains and not bring in the other  spider-man especially since they are  referencing them i think after this and  after these very clear editing mistakes  there's very very little doubt in a lot  of people's heads that toby maguire and  andrew garfield aren't in the movie and  again the scene with tom holland the  background the scaffolding everything  it's exactly like the leaked photos to  me that's enough proof right there then  you add the lizard getting punched in  the face by a ghost you add the arm that  wasn't edited out and the tobey maguire  or andrew garfield eyes in this one  scene i think it's pretty safe to say  that they're in the film but let me know  what you think and also let me know if  you think they're doing this on purpose  because i kind of think they might be  but let me know your thoughts in the  comments down below don't forget to  subscribe and hit that notif